# Cursor Rules for T81 Foundation

This file is a lightweight Cursor adapter. **Authoritative rules, research continuity boundaries, frozen contracts, and contribution guidelines live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md)** — read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ai-context/START_HERE.md` first before making changes.

## Cursor-Specific Workflow Hooks
- Locate the matching contract in `spec/` before editing implementation files (`isa/`, `vm/`, `fs/`, `kernel/axion/`, `lang/`, `src/crypto/`, `src/provider/`, `tools/`).
- Preserve frozen boundaries (`TISC v1.9.0`, `docs/governance/PUBLIC_API_LOCK.json` `v2.2.0`, `include/t81/**/*.hpp`) and all active research holds (`F01 M1–M6 STOP`, `SCG-08 Gate 2 NO-GO`, `H01` / Inv 10A `BLOCKED`, `AXION-AI-001 HD01–HD06`, `T81-AIOPT-001 M2 EXECUTION_BLOCKED`).
- Follow `DEC-004` (`docs/architecture/AI_OS_STRATIFIED_BLUEPRINT.md`): treat Horizon D Plane 2 neural OS helpers strictly as *Planned / Design Target* (`< 100 MB` RSS cap on `8 GB` M2 hosts), never as implemented.
- Prefer small, reviewable C++23/Python increments with targeted local builds/tests (`cmake --build build --target <target> -j4`, `ctest --test-dir build -R <regex>`) and local governance verification before opening a PR.
- Keep public claims evidence-bounded; never fabricate benchmarks, citations, or test runs.
